# UI component encapsulation plan

This checklist is the implementation source of truth for splitting SoulSearch's
current UI composition into cohesive, independently testable component modules.
The refactor is architectural and behavior-preserving: it must not redesign the
UI, change domain behavior, or complete unrelated items in `docs/project.todo`.

The selected granularity is one file per reusable or stateful widget/composite.
Trivial labels and one-purpose buttons remain inside the component that owns
them. Existing focused modules such as `stats_panel.lua`, `ui_tooltip.lua`, and
`stats_popover.lua` remain in place except for necessary import changes.

Record phase results in the `Execution evidence` table at the end of this
document. Do not mark a phase gate complete until its stated checks have passed.

## Target architecture

- [ ] Add an `internal/soulsearch/ui/` module namespace containing:
  - [ ] `modal_panel.lua` for reusable modal open, close, focus, and input
        capture behavior;
  - [ ] `filter_action_list.lua` for filter-row action hit-testing and
        dispatch;
  - [ ] `searchable_picker.lua` for the shared attribute, skill, and race
        picker structure;
  - [ ] `preset_picker.lua` for preset search, save, and selection UI;
  - [ ] `unit_scope_picker.lua` for the unit-scope popup;
  - [ ] `filter_panel.lua` for filter controls, active filters, picker
        composition, and filter-owned tooltip resolution;
  - [ ] `results_panel.lua` for query, result headings, result list, sorting,
        navigation, and result-owned tooltip resolution;
  - [ ] `main_window.lua` for state orchestration and component composition;
        and
  - [ ] `main_screen.lua` for screen lifecycle, registry participation,
        tooltip rendering, and frame persistence.
- [ ] Reduce `ui.lua` to the stable UI facade that exposes `open()` and
      `dismiss_all()`.
- [ ] Remove `ui_components.lua` after every consumer and test has migrated;
      do not leave a compatibility aggregator.
- [ ] Keep filtering, candidate collection, ranking, refresh ordering, and
      session persistence outside leaf UI components.
- [ ] Give Filter and Results components narrow host-facing APIs for updating
      choices/state, navigating results, and resolving component-owned
      tooltips.

## Behavior-preservation constraints

- [ ] Preserve the public `ui.open()` and `ui.dismiss_all()` contracts and all
      command/bootstrap behavior that calls them.
- [ ] Preserve existing view IDs and descendant exposure so refresh logic,
      tooltip lookup, tests, and current integrations continue to resolve the
      same controls.
- [ ] Preserve child creation and traversal order, including the Results query
      field's place in keyboard focus traversal and the result list's arrow-key
      behavior.
- [ ] Preserve every frame and boundary supplied by `ui_layout.lua`, including:
  - [ ] section dividers and panel placement;
  - [ ] filter action width and x-coordinate hitboxes;
  - [ ] Results header column hitboxes;
  - [ ] picker dimensions, overlap, and paint order; and
  - [ ] modal mouse capture and dismissal boundaries.
- [ ] Preserve all labels, colors, CP437 glyphs, shortcuts, tooltip text, and
      tooltip precedence.
- [ ] Preserve filter/picker open-state transitions, preset workflows, unit
      scope behavior, result selection retention, sort cycles, zoom behavior,
      and refresh cascades.
- [ ] Preserve window drag/resize handling, per-window session settings,
      frame persistence, multiple-window behavior, screen registration, and
      idempotent teardown.
- [ ] Keep `ui_refresh.apply()` and `SoulSearchRefreshOwner` unchanged. Main
      window refresh methods may delegate view updates to components, but the
      dispatcher contract and dependency order must not change.
- [ ] Register new modules before their consumers in `module_registry.lua` and
      keep reverse-order clearing safe for edited-module reloads.

## Explicit exclusions

- [ ] Do not implement the reusable columned list with sortable headers.
- [ ] Do not replace result or Stats headers with `CycleHotkeyLabel`; retain
      their existing separate sortable-header implementations.
- [ ] Do not evaluate or replace controls with alternative built-in DFHack
      widgets.
- [ ] Do not modify or close any remaining work in `docs/stats-popover.todo`.
- [ ] Do not add creatures-menu integration, scoped-window launch affordances,
      panel resizing, or automatic panel layout.
- [ ] Do not mark any unrelated `docs/project.todo` item complete.

## Phase 0 - Baseline and characterization

- [ ] Confirm the worktree state and record any pre-existing changes before
      source edits.
- [ ] Record the current module dependency order for `ui_components.lua`,
      `ui.lua`, `stats_panel.lua`, `ui_tooltip.lua`, and their consumers.
- [ ] Expand characterization tests before moving implementation:
  - [ ] exact top-level and recursive child order;
  - [ ] stable view IDs and descendant lookup;
  - [ ] keyboard focus/traversal and result-list cursor shortcuts;
  - [ ] modal open, close, right-click dismissal, and mouse capture;
  - [ ] picker visibility and overlap order;
  - [ ] filter action and Results header hit-testing;
  - [ ] tooltip source precedence and exact copy;
  - [ ] result selection, submission, sorting, and selection retention;
  - [ ] refresh delegation into Results, Stats, filters, and pickers;
  - [ ] drag/resize persistence and multiple-window settings isolation; and
  - [ ] screen registration and idempotent cleanup.
- [ ] Run the pre-refactor automated baseline:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.

### Phase 0 gate

- [ ] Tests fail if extraction changes composition, focus, geometry, input,
      tooltips, state transitions, refresh behavior, or lifecycle behavior.
- [ ] The automated baseline is green and recorded before modules move.

## Phase 1 - Establish the component namespace and leaf widgets

- [ ] Add the `internal/soulsearch/ui/` namespace without changing the public
      `internal/soulsearch/ui` facade path.
- [ ] Extract `ModalPanelWindow` into `ui/modal_panel.lua`:
  - [ ] export one documented class contract;
  - [ ] retain `is_open`, `on_open`, and `on_close` callback ownership;
  - [ ] preserve focus transitions and input consumption exactly; and
  - [ ] add focused tests for idempotent open/close and mouse behavior.
- [ ] Extract `FilterActionList` into `ui/filter_action_list.lua`:
  - [ ] retain action-choice snapshots and selected-row behavior;
  - [ ] retain scrolled-list index fallback;
  - [ ] preserve `FILTER_ACTION_WIDTH`-based hit-testing through
        `ui_layout.lua`; and
  - [ ] add focused click-boundary and callback tests.
- [ ] Add each module to `module_registry.lua` and the pure-Lua loader before
      migrating consumers.
- [ ] Keep compatibility imports in `ui_components.lua` only during this
      phase; do not duplicate class implementations.

### Phase 1 gate

- [ ] Leaf-widget tests pass through their new module paths.
- [ ] Existing `ui_components_test.lua` coverage remains green while consumers
      still use the temporary compatibility imports.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 2 - Extract picker and Filter Panel components

- [ ] Add `ui/searchable_picker.lua` as one configurable component used for
      attribute, skill, and race pickers:
  - [ ] accept stable IDs, title, visibility, key, query, close, and submit
        callbacks;
  - [ ] preserve each existing picker-specific view ID and keybinding;
  - [ ] preserve choice payloads and descriptor submission behavior; and
  - [ ] avoid moving filtering/query semantics into the component.
- [ ] Add `ui/preset_picker.lua` with the current save, query, custom preset,
      default preset, and role preset callback paths.
- [ ] Add `ui/unit_scope_picker.lua` with option-count-derived frames and the
      current scope-selection payload.
- [ ] Add `ui/filter_panel.lua` as a `ModalPanelWindow`-derived composite:
  - [ ] own creation of filter controls, `FilterActionList`, and all picker
        components;
  - [ ] retain the current host callback contract for state-changing actions;
  - [ ] expose narrow methods for active-filter and picker choice updates;
  - [ ] own filter-control, filter-action, and descriptor tooltip lookup; and
  - [ ] preserve the unit-scope picker as the last-painted overlapping child.
- [ ] Change `main_window.lua`'s future-facing contract only through delegation
      methods; leave domain filter state and refresh sequencing in the current
      main window until Phase 4.
- [ ] Split filter/picker characterization assertions into focused module tests
      and remove migrated assertions from `ui_components_test.lua`.

### Phase 2 gate

- [ ] Attribute, skill, race, preset, and unit-scope workflows behave exactly
      as before through the extracted Filter Panel.
- [ ] Filter action hitboxes, modal capture, focus, child order, and tooltips
      match the Phase 0 characterization.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 3 - Extract the Results Panel

- [ ] Add `ui/results_panel.lua` containing the Results-owned views:
  - [ ] query edit field;
  - [ ] title and underline;
  - [ ] existing sortable header implementation; and
  - [ ] result list.
- [ ] Define a narrow component API:
  - [ ] set query text without changing query semantics;
  - [ ] set choices and selected index;
  - [ ] return the selected result;
  - [ ] move the cursor by the requested delta; and
  - [ ] return the active Results header tooltip.
- [ ] Preserve host callbacks for query change, selection, submission/zoom,
      and sort transitions.
- [ ] Keep result formatting in `ui_format.lua`, column geometry in
      `ui_layout.lua`, and result-sort state/transition behavior in the main
      window.
- [ ] Preserve the query field's effective focus order when the flat view list
      becomes a component subtree.
- [ ] Migrate Results-owned tests from `ui_components_test.lua` and update
      main-window tests to assert delegation through the component API.

### Phase 3 gate

- [ ] Querying, selection refresh, zoom submission, cursor movement, sorting,
      row formatting, and header tooltips match the Phase 0 baseline.
- [ ] Results and Stats continue using their existing independent header
      implementations.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 4 - Extract the main Window and Screen

- [ ] Move `SoulSearchWindow` into `ui/main_window.lua`:
  - [ ] compose Results, Stats, Filter, tooltip-source, and window controls;
  - [ ] keep domain state, candidate/ranking orchestration, filter/preset
        operations, result-sort state, and session-setting writes here;
  - [ ] delegate component-owned view updates and tooltip queries through the
        new narrow APIs;
  - [ ] retain descendant view exposure where existing code/tests depend on
        stable IDs; and
  - [ ] preserve global input fallback order after superclass/component input.
- [ ] Move `SoulSearchScreen` into `ui/main_screen.lua`:
  - [ ] construct the main window and existing `SoulSearchTooltip` sibling;
  - [ ] preserve `focus_path='soulsearch'`;
  - [ ] retain screen-registry add/remove behavior; and
  - [ ] retain idempotent frame persistence and cleanup across dismissal,
        destruction, and reload.
- [ ] Keep screen placement policy and multiple-window creation behavior
      unchanged.
- [ ] Update `ui.lua` to import the extracted screen and expose only the stable
      facade/lifecycle functions.

### Phase 4 gate

- [ ] `gui/soulsearch`, scoped `ui.open(options)`, multiple windows, and
      `soulsearch reload` retain their existing contracts.
- [ ] Main-window keyboard, mouse, drag, resize, persistence, tooltip, refresh,
      and teardown tests match the baseline.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 5 - Remove the aggregate and harden module boundaries

- [ ] Migrate every remaining `ui_components` import to its owning module.
- [ ] Delete `ui_components.lua` and remove its old registry contract.
- [ ] Replace `tests/ui_components_test.lua` with focused per-component suites
      and register each suite explicitly in `tests/run.lua`.
- [ ] Update `tests/support/soulsearch_env.lua` with the minimum widget stubs
      and loaders required by the new modules; do not add
      `CycleHotkeyLabel` support in this refactor.
- [ ] Update `module_registry_test.lua` to assert complete dependency order:
  - [ ] dependency-free layout/format/state modules precede UI components;
  - [ ] leaf widgets precede picker/panel composites;
  - [ ] Filter, Results, Stats, and tooltip modules precede Main Window;
  - [ ] Main Window precedes Main Screen; and
  - [ ] Main Screen precedes the `ui.lua` facade.
- [ ] Search source, tests, and documentation for stale `ui_components`
      references and remove only references owned by this refactor.
- [ ] Confirm no behavior or implementation was copied into parallel modules
      during migration.

### Phase 5 gate

- [ ] Each reusable or stateful UI component has one implementation owner and
      one focused test boundary.
- [ ] No production or test code imports `ui_components.lua`.
- [ ] Reload order reconstructs all extracted classes without stale consumers.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 6 - Automated, packaged, and live validation

- [ ] Run the automated closure sequence separately and record every result:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Publish.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1` against the produced archive; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Verify the packaged mod contains every new component module, contains no
      deleted `ui_components.lua`, and has no stale duplicate implementation.
- [ ] Run an edited-module reload check that exercises the new registry order
      without reopening dismissed windows unexpectedly.
- [ ] Run a fortress-mode smoke pass:
  - [ ] open, close, and reopen the default SoulSearch window;
  - [ ] open multiple windows and verify independent state/frame persistence;
  - [ ] query and navigate Results with keyboard and mouse;
  - [ ] click each Results sort column boundary;
  - [ ] open/close the Filter Panel and every picker;
  - [ ] exercise filter action label edges and just outside each hitbox;
  - [ ] verify preset and unit-scope workflows;
  - [ ] verify filter, result-header, and Stats tooltips;
  - [ ] drag and resize the window; and
  - [ ] reload with windows open and confirm safe dismissal/reopening behavior.
- [ ] Review `git diff -- docs/project.todo docs/stats-popover.todo` and confirm
      neither unrelated checklist changed.

### Phase 6 gate

- [ ] Source, tests, reload registry, package contents, and live DFHack behavior
      all validate the component split.
- [ ] Automated results and live observations are recorded separately rather
      than treating packaging/tests as proof of interactive behavior.

## Definition of done

- [ ] `ui_components.lua` no longer exists or has consumers.
- [ ] Every reusable or stateful UI component has a cohesive module, documented
      host contract, and focused tests.
- [ ] `ui.lua` is a small stable facade; Main Window and Main Screen have
      separate implementation owners.
- [ ] Existing UI behavior, geometry, focus, hitboxes, state, persistence,
      refresh ordering, and lifecycle contracts are preserved.
- [ ] The sortable-column-list, built-in-widget evaluation, stats-popover,
      creatures-menu, and responsive-panel TODOs remain untouched.
- [ ] Build, tests, package verification, whitespace checks, and the live smoke
      pass are green with recorded evidence.

